id: pm-slack-standup-ozic
title: Canonicalize complete standup reads on pm CLI 2026.8.21
description: "Replace the deprecated list-all subprocess with one strict, full, doubly-unbounded canonical list --all request; delegate shared corpus proof to the public SDK; reject the remaining verified receipt gaps; exact-pin the current host; and prove installed npm and Bun behavior with real tracker data."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agents,cli-ux,complete-corpus,latest-cli,multi-agent
created_at: "2026-08-21T10:11:27.117Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-21T11:48:17.176Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-21T11:26:52.891Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-21T11:26:52.891Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 420
acceptance_criteria: "Create one canonical reader for every standup consumer; assert the exact canonical argv; require SDK certification plus narrow supplemental checks; validate fields used by the renderer; exact-pin development pm CLI/SDK 2026.8.21 while proving the declared behavior floor; add fresh packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx acceptance with real items and no deprecated stderr; update docs, changelog, CI and release gates; retain independent exact-coverage and privacy blockers"
definition_of_ready: Main is clean at 2d0077a; 59 complete tracker items were read; 145 tests and current release gate pass; the deprecated runtime call and current receipt gaps are reproduced.
reviewer: greptile
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: 2026-08-canonical-readers
release: next
reporter: codex
severity: high
environment: "pm-slack-standup 2026.8.17, pm CLI 2026.8.21, Node 22.19.0"
repro_steps: "Run the current standup reader and inspect its argv: it invokes list-all without strict-read, full projection, or either unbounded output control."
resolution: "Replaced the deprecated reader with one SDK-certified canonical complete-corpus boundary, exact-pinned the supported host and workflow actions, added real packed npm/Bun/current/minimum/external-host and Windows acceptance, and hardened read-only CI credentials."
expected_result: "A standup is rendered only from a structurally valid, SDK-certified, complete tracker corpus using canonical CLI syntax."
actual_result: "The final implementation head 19d4640 passed 152 tests, 73 documented declarations across five executable TypeScript files, five packed acceptance scenarios, zero production vulnerabilities, a nine-file pack, and GitHub CI on Node 22.18.0, Node 26, and Windows. Configured index.ts coverage is 89.97 percent lines, 88.32 percent branches, and 91.27 percent functions, not exact all-source 100/100/100/100. One valid CodeRabbit security finding was fixed and resolved. Exact-head CodeRabbit, Sourcery, Cubic, Greptile, and Gemini review availability remained limited or silent and is not approval. Items pm-slack-standup-7t31 and pm-slack-standup-g2vl plus GitHub issue 45 still prohibit merge and publication."
affected_version: pm-slack-standup 2026.8.17
component: fetchAllItems complete-corpus reader
customer_impact: "A partial or unverifiable tracker read can under-report active work in an automated standup, while alias warnings pollute agent stderr."
notes[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-21T10:13:33.108Z",codex,"Red-first evidence: new complete-list contract tests require one exact canonical argv, public SDK rejection for malformed/filter/paging/projection/count/identity evidence, narrow pm-cli 2026.8.21 supplemental receipt checks, and renderer-field validation. npm run build:test fails because COMPLETE_LIST_COMMAND_ARGUMENTS and readCompleteStandupItems do not yet exist; implementation has not been added."
  "2026-08-21T10:31:29.856Z",codex,"Green implementation evidence: npm run release:check passes. Configured index.ts coverage is 89.97 percent lines, 88.32 percent branches, and 91.27 percent functions; this is explicitly not exact all-source 100/100/100/100. The packed matrix initialized fresh trackers through npm and Bun on pm CLI 2026.8.21 and 2026.8.20, created one in-progress and one open item, installed the packed extension, exported one standup, reconciled two rendered items to the two tracker items, and found no deprecated list-all diagnostic. CI and release changelog reads now pass both unbounded controls; PR CI runs both installed acceptance gates."
  "2026-08-21T10:35:15.193Z",codex,"A dedicated Windows PR job now type-checks, compiles the test graph, runs the launcher contract suite, and executes the same packed npm/Bun current/minimum matrix through real Windows launchers. This is pending GitHub exact-head execution and is not yet counted as green evidence."
  "2026-08-21T10:37:55.511Z",codex,"First exact-head Windows execution exposed three additional POSIX-shell fixture tests that lacked the established posixOnly declaration. Their failures were ENOENT/cmd launch artifacts rather than product behavior; the real project-local pm integration passed on Windows. The three tests now declare the same explicit Windows skip as every other #!/bin/sh fixture, while the Windows job continues to the real packed npm/Bun launcher matrix."
  "2026-08-21T10:41:13.088Z",codex,"Second Windows run reached the packed gate and reproduced Node spawnSync EINVAL when launching npm.cmd directly. The acceptance runner now executes npm-cli.js and npx-cli.js through process.execPath, preserving discrete argv and avoiding shell:true while exercising the same user-facing npm/npx code. Bun remains a direct executable launch. Local typecheck and all four packed scenarios pass after the change."
  "2026-08-21T10:44:47.718Z",codex,"Greptile P1 claimed a peer-only top-level SDK import would break GitHub or copied installs. Exact reproduction disproved the runtime claim: pm install materializes the extension with a symlink from its node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli to the active external host, and standup export rendered real data with no tracker-local node_modules. The review still exposed an acceptance visibility gap, so a fifth mandatory npm-global-current scenario now proves this layout. The finding was down-voted and answered inline with the evidence; no duplicate runtime CLI dependency was introduced."
  "2026-08-21T10:54:23.493Z",codex,"Exact head 337bacf GitHub CI completed green: Node 22.18.0 and Node 26 each ran the mandatory release surfaces; windows-acceptance-launcher passed its native launcher suite and all five packed scenarios in 9m02s. The earlier pending-Windows note is superseded by this evidence."
  "2026-08-21T11:03:00.324Z",codex,"author=codex,text=Late CodeRabbit exact-head review found tag-pinned actions and persisted checkout credentials in the new Windows job. Applied the finding across both CI jobs and immutable-pin consistency across release workflow, added executable workflow security regression tests, and reran release:check green with 152 tests and all five packed acceptance scenarios."
  "2026-08-21T11:26:52.214Z",codex,"Final review audit at implementation head 19d4640 found one valid CodeRabbit workflow-hardening issue. Exact action SHA pins,persist-credentials false on both CI checkouts,and mandatory regression tests fixed it. Node 22.18.0,Node 26,and Windows acceptance passed; the CodeRabbit thread is resolved. Exact-head CodeRabbit was rate-limited,Sourcery and Cubic quota-limited,and Greptile and Gemini supplied no substantive exact-head response,so these are limitations rather than approvals."
  "2026-08-21T11:48:17.151Z",codex,"Clarification after exact-head review: 19d4640 is deliberately named as the final code-bearing implementation head. Commit 010935e only appended the scoped closure evidence and changelog. A commit cannot persist its own eventual SHA; PR 46 is the authoritative exact-head pointer for the later review-fix commit. The coverage baseline remains 89.97/88.32/91.27 and the independent blockers remain open."
